<!doctype html><html lang="en-US"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Trust-Worthy Method | Project Unveiled</title><meta name="description" content="The public investigation method used by Trust-Worthy AI."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/trust-worthy/assets/trust-worthy.css"></head><body><header class="site-header"><div class="container nav"><a class="brand" href="/">PROJECT <span>UNVEILED</span></a><div><a href="/trust-worthy/">Trust-Worthy</a><a href="/trust-worthy/case.php?id=TW-CASE-000001">Truth Trial #000001</a></div></div></header><main><section class="hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Public research standard</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5.4rem)">Investigate before you conclude.</h1><p class="lead">Trust-Worthy does not outsource difficult claims to a fact-check label. It follows evidence toward its source, tests rival explanations, searches for reasons its own conclusion may be wrong, and shows where certainty ends.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="grid"><div class="panel"><h3>1. Define the claim</h3><p class="muted">Break broad questions into propositions that can actually be examined.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>2. Expose assumptions</h3><p class="muted">Identify premises hidden inside the wording of the question.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>3. Hunt sources</h3><p class="muted">Prefer primary and earliest available evidence over repetition and summaries.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>4. Establish provenance</h3><p class="muted">Ask who created the evidence, when, where it came from, and whether its attribution is disputed.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>5. Trace source lineage</h3><p class="muted">Collapse apparent independent confirmations when they ultimately derive from the same source.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>6. Restore context</h3><p class="muted">Chronology, audience, genre, politics, culture, and surrounding text matter.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>7. Examine language</h3><p class="muted">Where interpretation depends on Greek, Hebrew, Aramaic, Latin, or another language, compare wording and translation choices.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>8. Seek corroboration</h3><p class="muted">Count genuinely independent evidence, not popularity or repetition.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>9. Attack the preliminary finding</h3><p class="muted">A separate adversarial pass must build the strongest credible case against the initial conclusion.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>10. Test alternatives</h3><p class="muted">Compare competing hypotheses rather than forcing every question into a binary.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>11. Audit the logic</h3><p class="muted">Separate documented evidence, inference, interpretation, and speculation.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>12. Record uncertainty</h3><p class="muted">If surviving evidence cannot resolve a question, say so plainly.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Theology mode</div><h2>Christ-consistency is a separate analysis.</h2><p class="lead">For theological cases, Trust-Worthy may compare an interpretation with the recorded teachings and conduct of Jesus. That analysis is labeled as theological coherence, not presented as direct access to God's mind or as a substitute for historical evidence.</p><div class="notice">No doctrine, denomination, founder, skeptic, Project Unveiled claim, or prior Trust-Worthy finding receives protected status.</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Possible outcomes</div><h2>Not everything becomes “true” or “false.”</h2><div class="grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Unveiled</h3><p class="muted">The evidence meaningfully supports an interpretation.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Bunk Book</h3><p class="muted">A claim materially fails provenance, chronology, context, logic, or evidence testing.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Mystery Book</h3><p class="muted">Available evidence is insufficient to responsibly resolve the question.</p></div></div></div></section></main><footer><div class="container"><a href="/trust-worthy/case.php?id=TW-CASE-000001">Examine the first Truth Trial</a> · <a href="/trust-worthy/challenge.php?id=TW-CASE-000001">Challenge it</a></div></footer></body></html>